  "Question": "The marked price of a book was \\(30\\%\\) less than the suggested retail price. Alice purchased the book for half the marked price at a Fiftieth Anniversary sale. What percent of the suggested retail price did Alice pay?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(25\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(30\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(35\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(60\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(65\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "A price \\(30\\%\\) below retail is \\(100\\%-30\\%=70\\%\\) of retail. Alice then pays half of that marked price, so she pays\n\\[\n\\frac12\\cdot70\\%=35\\%\n\\]\nof the suggested retail price. The answer is \\(35\\%\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
